## 6. Code Examples

### 1. Canonical Premium Button (Tailwind v4 + Framer Motion)
```tsx
import { motion, HTMLMotionProps } from "framer-motion"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
import { Loader2 } from "lucide-react"

interface ButtonProps extends HTMLMotionProps<"button"> {
  variant?: "primary" | "ghost" | "danger" | "glass"
  size?: "sm" | "md" | "lg"
  isLoading?: boolean
}

export function Button({ 
  className, variant = "primary", size = "md", isLoading, children, ...props 
}: ButtonProps) {
  const variants = {
    primary: "bg-indigo-600 text-white shadow-[0_4px_14px_0_rgba(99,102,241,0.39)] hover:shadow-[0_6px_20px_rgba(99,102,241,0.23)] hover:bg-indigo-500",
    ghost: "bg-transparent text-zinc-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5",
    glass: "bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-lg border border-white/10 text-white hover:bg-white/10",
    danger: "bg-red-500/10 text-red-500 hover:bg-red-500/20"
  }
  
  const sizes = {
    sm: "h-8 px-3 text-xs",
    md: "h-10 px-5 text-sm",
    lg: "h-12 px-8 text-base"
  }

  return (
    <motion.button
      whileHover={{ scale: 1.02 }}
      whileTap={{ scale: 0.98 }}
      className={cn(
        "relative rounded-xl font-medium flex items-center justify-center gap-2 transition-colors",
        "focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-500 focus-visible:outline-none",
        variants[variant], 
        sizes[size], 
        className
      )}
      disabled={isLoading || props.disabled}
      {...props}
    >
      {isLoading && <Loader2 className="w-4 h-4 animate-spin" />}
      {children}
    </motion.button>
  )
}
```

### 2. Micro-interaction: Reply Swipe (Framer Motion)
```tsx
// This goes inside MessageBubble wrapper
const [dragX, setDragX] = useState(0)

<motion.div
  drag="x"
  dragConstraints={{ left: 0, right: 0 }}
  onDrag={(e, info) => {
    // Only allow dragging right
    if (info.offset.x > 0) setDragX(info.offset.x)
  }}
  onDragEnd={(e, info) => {
    if (info.offset.x > 100) {
      onReply()
    }
    setDragX(0)
  }}
  style={{ x: dragX }} // Use motion value for performance in real app
>
  {/* Drag Indicator Icon that appears behind */}
  <div style={{ opacity: dragX / 100 }} className="absolute left-[-40px]">
    <ReplyIcon /> 
  </div>
  <MessageContent />
</motion.div>
```

---

## 7. Migration Strategy: Component-by-Component features
Instead of a "Big Bang" rewrite, we will use the **Strangler Fig Pattern**:
1.  **New Components Dir**: Create `src/components/design-system/...`.
2.  **Parallel Implementation**: Build `ButtonV2`, `InputV2`.
3.  **Adoption**: Pick ONE high-traffic view (e.g., [SettingsModal](file:///f:/projects/Vibely/frontend/src/components/settings/settings-modal.tsx#25-153)) to convert fully to V2.
4.  **Verification**: Verify visual regression and accessibility.
5.  **Rollout**: Propagate to [ChatWindow](file:///f:/projects/Vibely/frontend/src/components/chat/chat-window.tsx#34-576).

## 8. Risks & Mitigations
*   **Risk**: Performance regression from heavy animations.
    *   *Mitigation*: Use `will-change` extensively; test on low-end mobile; provide "Reduce Motion" setting (already in SettingsModal plan).
*   **Risk**: Tailwind v4 Compatibility.
    *   *Mitigation*: It is in Alpha/Beta. If breaking bugs occur, revert to v3.4 (Shadcn standard) with minimal logic changes.
*   **Risk**: Accessibility oversight with custom "Glass" components.
    *   *Mitigation*: Use `radix-ui` primitives for all interactive states (dialogs, tooltips) to guarantee ARIA compliance.

